        "title": "7. Reproduce locally with a single solver",
        "content": "Tested implementation: Python 3.12 with numpy, numba, fpylll, cysignals, ecdsa. The optional screenshot requires scipy and Pillow.\n\nFrom WSL/Linux:\n\n~~~bash\nsource /home/nata/ctf_env/bin/activate\npython3 -m pip install numpy numba fpylll cysignals ecdsa scipy pillow\n~~~\n\nPut solve.py in the same folder as hall-of-mirrors.zip and run:\n\n~~~bash\npython3 -u solve.py --spectrogram 2>&1 | tee solve.log\n~~~\n\nThe script validates the archive's SHA-256, extracts the WAV if necessary, validates the carrier CRC, executes MVM1, verifies all 48 signatures, recovers the private key with LLL/CVP, decrypts the sealed blob, and writes intermediates to hall_output/.\n\nIf the WAV is already unpacked in hall/:\n\n~~~bash\npython3 -u solve.py --wav hall/hall-of-mirrors.wav --spectrogram\n~~~\n\nOptional custom seed:\n\n~~~bash\npython3 solve.py --wav hall/hall-of-mirrors.wav --seed 0x9C4F1E7A3B50D682\n~~~\n\nExpected terminal output (validated against the supplied WAV):\n\n~~~text\n[+] WAV=hall-of-mirrors.wav data_offset=216 data_size=299520000; samples=149760000\n[+] Spectrogram seed K=0x9c4f1e7a3b50d682\n[+] MirrorStego magic OK, payload=6266 bytes, CRC-32=e2046fb1 OK\n[+] MVM1 HLT at pc=0x0340, instructions=20395, PCH=8, SMC=3\n[+] MVM1 output=5083 bytes\n[+] TLV record count=58, ECDSA tuples=48, sealed=33 bytes\n[+] secp256k1, ECDSA signatures verified=48\n[+] LLL/CVP dimension=41; L=12; nonce upper bound=244 bits\n[+] Private key validated against Q and 48 bounded nonces; max_nonce_bits=244\n[+] KDF key32=a34c6fd7c69371c4c72e14d046b00a2c147f00067dfff01aaec8ef0097d10fdc\n[+] Decrypted 33 bytes; flag syntax verified\n<FLAG>hiCTF{h1dd3n_numb3r_l4ttice_le4k}</FLAG>\n~~~\n\nArtifacts in hall_output/:\n\n| File | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| hall-of-mirrors.wav | Unpacked original audio, when input is ZIP |\n| seed_spectrogram.png | Audio-derived proof of K (when --spectrogram) |\n| carrier_payload.bin | 6,266-byte MVM1 image |\n| vm_output.bin | 5,083-byte TLV blob |\n| private_key.txt | Scalar recovered by LLL/CVP |\n| unsealed.bin | Decrypted 33-byte flag |\n\nFor convenience, the distributed ZIP bundle also includes seed_spectrogram.png."
