      {
        "title": "8. Root cause and interpretation",
        "content": "The WAV steganography and self-modifying VM add analysis friction, but the decisive cryptographic flaw is **biased ECDSA nonce generation**. Twelve fixed nonce bits across 48 signatures give enough bounded modular relations for a lattice-based private-key recovery. Once d is known, the custom KDF and stream cipher offer no independent security barrier because their key is deterministically derived from d.\n\nThe exploit does not involve network access, an operating-system memory corruption bug, a secp256k1 discrete-log break, or a guessed flag. All substantive stages are validated using data emitted from the supplied archives.\n\n**Final flag:** hiCTF{h1dd3n_numb3r_l4ttice_le4k}"
      }
